    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Maglev as a bond graph.** Electrical 1-junction Jc (coil current): amplifier MSe Amp (+-60 V rail in Sat), coil resistance Rc, current detector Imeas and the coil port of EM. EM is the two-port IC-field electromagnet: co-energy W' = L(h)*i^2/2 with L(h) = L_inf + 2*alpha/h, so its gap port carries F = alpha*i^2/h^2. Mechanical 1-junction Jb (ball velocity, down positive): gravity Se Grav, ball mass I Ball, the armature port of EM and the position sensor. The detectors give the field's port powers: coil voltage Vcoil (De on the 0-junction Jv) times Imeas, attraction Fmag (De on Jf) times ball velocity Vball; EM/W - Eel/y - Emech/y stays at W(0).",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 1100,
        "w": 1100,
        "h": 110
      },
      {
        "id": "a2",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Cascade.** Outer: gain-scheduled PID on the IR measurement plus trim feedforward c_trim*h -> current setpoint; its gains are designed with the 1 kHz sample-and-hold, the inner loop and a 5 ms derivative filter in the phase budget. Inner: PI (Kp = L*1000 rad/s, Ti = L/R) -> voltage command.",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 560,
        "w": 640,
        "h": 80,
        "color": "blue"
      }
    ]
  },
  "settings": {
    "t_start": 0.0,
    "t_end": 1.4,
    "solver": "auto",
    "reltol": 1e-09,
    "abstol": 1e-12,
    "max_step": null,
    "output": {
      "mode": "points",
      "points": 2801
    },
    "event_limit": 10000
